
%9Syntax:%9

TRACKBAR%|
TRACKBAR GOTO%|
TRACKBAR KEEP%|
TRACKBAR MARK%|
TRACKBAR MARKVISIBLE%|
TRACKBAR MARKALL%|
TRACKBAR REMOVE%|
TRACKBAR REMOVEALL%|
TRACKBAR REDRAW%|

%9Parameters:%9

    GOTO:        Scrolls the active window to the trackbar line (same as
                 /TRACKBAR without arguments).
    KEEP:        The next time you leave the active window, the line stays
                 where it is (once).
    MARK:        Removes the old line and draws a new one at the bottom of
                 the active window (same as /MARK).
    MARKVISIBLE: Like MARK, for all visible windows (split screen).
    MARKALL:     Like MARK, for all windows.
    REMOVE:      Removes the line from the active window.
    REMOVEALL:   Removes the lines from all windows.
    REDRAW:      Redraws all lines using the current settings.

%9Description:%9

    The trackbar.pl script draws a horizontal line in the window you are
    leaving, so when you come back you can see where you stopped reading.
    The previous line in that window is removed. A command of the
    trackbar.pl script.

    The line is never logged (level NEVER) and does not appear in empty
    windows or in windows from trackbar_ignore_windows (except with /MARK
    and /TRACKBAR MARK). Before /UPGRADE and when the script is unloaded
    all lines are removed, and after a terminal resize they are redrawn.

    GOTO scrolls with /SCROLLBACK GOTO to the time the line was drawn (to
    the second). When the window has no line, "No trackbar found in this
    window" is printed.

%9Settings:%9

    trackbar_string = ─
        Character or string the line is made of ('-' on a terminal
        without UTF-8).
    trackbar_style = %%K
        Colour of the line, in irssi format notation.
    trackbar_ignore_windows =
        Windows without a line: names, numbers, or channel and query
        names, separated by spaces or commas.
    trackbar_use_status_window = ON
        Also draw the line in the (status) window.
    trackbar_print_timestamp = OFF
        Print a timestamp in front of the line.
    trackbar_require_seen = OFF
        ON = the line moves only after you have seen it (scrolled to it).
    trackbar_all_manual = OFF
        ON = the line moves only with /MARK.

%9Examples:%9

    /TRACKBAR
    /TRACKBAR MARKALL
    /BIND meta-t command trackbar

%9See also:%9 BIND, MARK, SCROLLBACK

